    <h2>Discuss Topics in Effective Altruism</h2>
    <p>For the fall 2026 semester, Impact Lab meetings will be on Sundays from 2:00&ndash;3:00 pm in DUC 241. Everyone is welcome to attend, including those who are new to effective altruism.</p>
    <p>Impact Lab meetings aim to deepen participants' understanding of effective altruism concepts and foster a collaborative environment for figuring out how to have an impactful career. Through structured discussions and hands-on activities, Impact Lab equips members to critically engage with complex global issues and translate EA principles into concrete career actions.</p>
    <p>Previous topics have included:</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>How to Have a High-Impact Career</li>
      <li>A History of Nuclear Near-Misses</li>
      <li>Forecasting</li>
      <li>Animal Welfare vs. Global Health as a Cause Area</li>
      <li>Biosecurity</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
